# Changes: regenerated against the post-series 151.0.7922.137 tree with 007 already applied. Three
#          hunks needed it and the rest applied unchanged:
#            * element.cc #1 failed outright -- 151 added
#              components/viz/common/surfaces/tracked_element_rects.h and
#              third_party/blink/public/mojom/scroll/scroll_enums.mojom-blink.h to the include block.
#            * document.cc #1 and #3 landed with fuzz 2. Both outcomes were read back and were
#              correct (base/command_line.h after base/auto_reset.h, ungoogled_switches.h between
#              cc/input/scroll_snap_data.h and mojo/.../wtf_hash_util.h, and the noise-factor block
#              replacing the RuntimeEnabledFeatures one in the Document constructor), then
#              regenerated with diff -u.
#          Forward-applied to a pristine scratch copy afterwards to confirm zero fuzz and zero
#          offset, since the build tree already carried the result.
#
# getClientRects / getBoundingClientRect noise, driven by --fingerprint=<seed>. It repurposes
# ungoogled's Document::noise_factor_{x,y}_ from a multiplicative factor (1 +/- 1.5e-6, randomised
# per Document with base::RandDouble) into a seed-derived ADDITIVE offset:
# hash("<seed>offset_x") mapped to [-0.5, 0.5] and scaled by 0.002, i.e. +/-0.001 px. Element and
# Range apply it with rect.Offset(...) / quad.Offset(...) instead of Scale(...), and QuadF gains an
# Offset method that no-ops on a degenerate quad.
#
# Measured 2026-08-21, --fingerprint=7, against the zero-patch control in the same host state:
#
#   getClientRects()[0].x  0 -> 0.0005369044956751168     (main frame and cross-site iframe alike)
#                      .y  0 -> 0.0004479514609556645
#                  width   100      -> 100      unchanged
#                  height  20       -> 20       unchanged
#   seed 8      x = -0.00010738246055552736,  seed 424242  x = 0.0002731819695327431
#
# Deterministic, seed-derived, identical across realms. Three properties of the design are worth
# knowing before anyone relies on it, all measured rather than inferred:
#
#   1. It is a CONSTANT TRANSLATION of the whole document, not per-element noise. Widths, heights
#      and the difference between any two rects are bit-identical to the unpatched engine -- and
#      those are what getClientRects fingerprinting actually reads.
#   2. It is trivially detectable. Layout-derived rect coordinates in stock Chromium are LayoutUnit
#      multiples of 1/64, so Number.isInteger(rect.x * 64) is true there and false here; on a
#      margin:0 body, document.body.getBoundingClientRect().x is 0 upstream and 0.000536... here.
#   3. ShouldSkipClientRectsOffset() exempts position:absolute elements whose top and left are zero
#      or fixed, so a single page can compare an exempt element (quantised) against a static one
#      (not) -- an internal contradiction that is a stronger signal than either half.
#
# Recorded, not fixed: see Veil/docs/MIGRATION-UNGOOGLED.md 5.1l.
#
# Note for anyone reading 015 next to this: 014 pairs a small value with an additive call, which is
# correct. 015 computes the same kind of value and hands it to the MULTIPLICATIVE
# TextMetrics::Shuffle, which is why measureText collapses -- see Veil/docs/MIGRATION-UNGOOGLED.md
# 5.1h.
#
